# What `vercel deploy` must not upload.
#
# The CLI is linked at the repository root (`.vercel/repo.json`), so a deploy
# run from `apps/store` or `apps/studio` still uploads from here. Without this
# file it falls back to the `.gitignore` of the directory it was run in, and
# those directories have none, so it packed the whole tree: 2.5 GB of Turbo
# cache and a 723 MB Next build, which trips the 100 MB per-file limit.
#
# Vercel builds from the committed source, so none of this is needed there.

# dependencies
node_modules

# build output and caches
.next
.turbo
dist
out
*.tsbuildinfo

# tests
playwright-report
test-results
coverage

# env files
.env*
!.env.example

# local-only documents and notes
working
.scratch
.sanity

# os
.DS_Store
